      "skill_shake",
      "boss and race skill procedurals",
      "shield / stack / heal diff branches"
    ]
  },
  "design_corrections_forced_by_evidence": [
    {
      "what": "A missing TARGET actor now degrades instead of dropping the cue.",
      "why": "With a real adapter the cues are asynchronous. The renderer prunes a dead unit's actor on the next refresh while the killer's impact and damage-number cues are still queued behind its 0.12s windup, so the killing blow's number - the one the player most needs - was being dropped. 8 drops in round 1 and 7 in round 2 before the fix, 0 after. A missing SOURCE actor still drops.",
      "follows": "checklist 4.2 degrade-don't-drop, same as a missing profile"
    },
    {
      "what": "The dying unit's actor is claimed at enqueue time, not at cue playback.",
      "why": "Checklist 4.3 keeps a dying unit's in-flight action, so its own death cue queues behind it and the renderer freed the body first. An earlier attempt to interrupt the in-flight action was reverted because it contradicted 4.3 and the D2 death_cancel_queue assertion; owning the corpse lifetime is the correct fix.",
      "follows": "checklist 3, 'play the death animation, THEN unregister the actor'"
    },
    {
      "what": "detach_actor_for_death keeps the registry entry until the fade ends.",
      "why": "The actor is still on screen during the death animation, so its anchors stay valid."
    }
  ],
